teather (0.1.0-7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Raise the relay concurrency ceiling from 64 to 256 flows (tun2proxy
    --max-sessions and the phone-side SOCKS server). The 2026-08-30 live test
    hit the old limit repeatedly under a full-desktop failover; long-lived
    udpgw streams also consume a slot each.

 -- Teather Project <noreply@example.invalid>  Sat, 30 Aug 2026 18:00:00 +0000

teather (0.1.0-6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * UDP support (D-024). tun2proxy is now built with its `udpgw` feature and run
    with `--udpgw-server`; the phone's new UdpGatewayServer terminates the
    framed-datagram stream over the existing SOCKS connection and forwards each
    datagram on the selected upstream. No second ADB forward, no VpnService, no
    packet stack on the phone. IPv6 UDP is still refused. NOTE: this package
    requires the tun2proxy binary rebuilt with `--features udpgw`.
  * `teather upstream` now rebinds the phone's relay upstream with no teardown,
    using the Android app's new ACTION_RECONFIGURE (versionCode 3, 0.1.0-p1.1).
    The SOCKS listener, teather0, the tunnel, routes, and DNS all stay up and
    established sessions keep their transport, so no connection sees a gap.
  * The Android launcher icon now matches the Linux client artwork, and the
    app's on-screen description no longer carries stale "P0 / TCP CONNECT only"
    wording.

 -- Teather Project <noreply@example.invalid>  Sat, 30 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000

teather (0.1.0-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * D-023: `teather upstream auto|cellular|wifi|ethernet` (also SetUpstream on
    D-Bus and a GUI dropdown) picks which of the phone's transports the relay
    uses. Switching while connected restarts only the phone's relay binding;
    teather0, the tunnel, routes, and DNS are untouched.

 -- Teather Project <noreply@example.invalid>  Sat, 30 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000

teather (0.1.0-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * D-022: NetworkManager owns the non-persistent teather0 tun connection from
    creation (tun.owner delegation), replacing D-021's externally-assumed
    interface and its non-functional Reapply DNS.
  * DNS is now additive and non-exclusive: the physical link's resolver stays
    first while it is present; the Teather sentinel is only used once it is gone.
  * Remove the setuid-root helper and its polkit action; the packet engine runs
    unprivileged. Restore NoNewPrivileges=yes on the user unit.
  * Add the auto-failover setting (teather failover on|off), default on.

 -- Teather Project <noreply@example.invalid>  Sat, 29 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000

